   "source": [
    "## 12. Conclusion — Review 2 Part B\n",
    "Among the ten algorithms evaluated, Bagging with a Decision Tree achieved the best baseline performance, with an accuracy of 79.95%, a weighted F1-score of 0.8009, and a weighted ROC-AUC of 0.9355. We also applied hyperparameter tuning using GridSearchCV, but the tuned models did not improve their baseline test F1-scores.
     Overall, the results demonstrate that ensemble learning, particularly Bagging, can effectively identify steel plate defect categories."
   ]
